WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.680
"It is the first mild day of March:" A
robin sings from a tall larch by the door.

2
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.860
Inside, a book lies open on the table.

3
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.730
Then a voice calls: "Come
forth and feel the sun."

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.550
And: "And bring no book".

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.240
Leave the book behind?

6
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.780
So is Wordsworth against learning?

7
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.290
In this mission, you'll
go back to spring 1798,

8
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.380
when he wrote this to his sister Dorothy,

9
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.560
at Alfoxden in Somerset.

10
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.740
You'll test one bold claim the poem makes.

11
00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:34.170
Is it as anti-learning as it sounds?

12
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.420
And you'll see how the poem
circles back to its invitation.

13
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:42.160
Your mission: decide whether
Wordsworth is anti-learning.
